{
  "comment": [
    "TM-2's corpus. `src/pypi/filename.rs` is a hand-rolled PEP 427/625 splitter, and",
    "a misattributed filename would be judged as some other version — which is how a",
    "version-specific block gets escaped. Every case below must yield either the",
    "version named here or an exclusion; none may yield a different version.",
    "",
    "`version` is the spelling the filename carries, or null when the file cannot be",
    "named at all and must be excluded. `listed` is whether the file appears in the",
    "served listing when `friendly-bard` version `1.0` is blocked — so it is false",
    "for every excluded file, false for every spelling PEP 440 says *is* 1.0, and",
    "true for every genuinely different release.",
    "",
    "Only the `friendly-bard` cases take part in the end-to-end half; the others are",
    "there because a version-like or heavily punctuated project name is exactly what",
    "a naive splitter mis-reads."
  ],
